-- Every way of asking means the same thing (spec 3.2).

please show "please"
kindly show "kindly"
would you show "would you"
would you please show "would you please"
would you kindly show "would you kindly"
if you would show "if you would"
if you would please show "if you would please"
if you would be so kind show "if you would be so kind"
if you would be so kind as to show "if you would be so kind as to"
if it is not too much trouble show "if it is not too much trouble"

-- One courtesy word can cover a run of actions (rule 3).
please:
    show "one"
    show "courtesy"
    show "word"
thank you for everything
